From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DVDInputStreamBluray: a resume point without the disc's
 state plays the main title

A Blu-ray resumed from the disc image itself, not from one of its
playlists, finds the playlist it was stopped in from the player state
kept with the resume point. A resume point written without that state
(by another client of a shared library, a library sync, or JSON-RPC)
leaves GetTitleFromState() with nothing to read: Open() logs "failed to
get title info" and the film does not play at all.

A resume point with no state now plays the longest title from the saved
time, which is the title the disc is played with when it has no menu. A
state naming a playlist the disc does not have still fails as before.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
index 4716e8df61..05f12538cc 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
@@ -373,7 +373,8 @@ bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::Open()
   else if (resumable && m_item.GetStartOffset() == STARTOFFSET_RESUME && m_item.IsResumable())
   {
     m_navmode = false;
-    m_titleInfo = GetTitleFromState(m_item.GetVideoInfoTag()->GetResumePoint().playerState);
+    const std::string& state = m_item.GetVideoInfoTag()->GetResumePoint().playerState;
+    m_titleInfo = state.empty() ? GetTitleLongest() : GetTitleFromState(state);
   }
   else
   {
